      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SCARLETTI (5) went off the boil at the end of his last prep, and he usually comes to hand quickly. He has won the latest of his tune-up trials, and it is important to note the booking of top hoop Anthony Darmanin fresh. Watch the market moves closely, and we put him on top of an even field. WOLF JUNIOR (4) progressed to this grade by winning his penultimate start here by a neck, and then failed to fire here 12 days ago. With less time between runs, he is worth another chance, so include him in all combos. KAKIA (1) has been racing consistently this season, and was third as the favourite in a similar field to this here last time out when shouldering 62.5kg. He carries 4kg less this time thanks to an apprentice claim, and with luck from a wide draw, he can figure in the top 4 again. SEVILLANA (3) drops back in class after a modest effort here nearly 5 weeks ago. A 4kg claim will help offset the weight rise, and she can bounce straight back into the money. ZURICH (2) has top 4 claims.",
